version: 1.0.0
description: MCP server — AI authoring interface for Atelier animations with 70 tools
context:
  - This is the primary AI interface — all animation authoring goes through these MCP tools
  - In-memory document store accumulates state across tool calls in a session
  - Tools provide structured error responses from Zod validation for AI-readable feedback
  - Preview returns resolved frame data (not rendered image) for AI comprehension
components:
  mcp-store:
    description: In-memory document store — Map-based CRUD for AtelierDocument instances across tool calls, with onChange event emitter for the LLM↔human live-mutation bridge (task #10)
    file: src/store.ts
    signals:
      - '!doc-change'
  mcp-document-tools:
    description: Document lifecycle tools — create, info, load (YAML), export (YAML), list
    file: src/tools/document.ts
  mcp-layer-tools:
    description: Layer management tools — add, edit, remove, list, reorder
    file: src/tools/layers.ts
  mcp-shape-tools:
    description: Shape visual tools — set_shape, set_fill, set_stroke on shape-type layers
    file: src/tools/shapes.ts
  mcp-state-tools:
    description: State management tools — add, edit, remove, list animation states
    file: src/tools/states.ts
  mcp-delta-tools:
    description: Delta animation tools — add, edit, remove deltas with overlap validation, apply presets
    file: src/tools/deltas.ts
  mcp-preset-tools:
    description: Preset tools — define reusable animation presets, list available presets
    file: src/tools/presets.ts
  mcp-preview-tools:
    description: Preview tools — validate document schema + overlaps, preview resolved frame data
    file: src/tools/preview.ts
  mcp-template-tools:
    description: Template MCP tools — instantiate_template, find_variables
    file: src/tools/templates.ts
  mcp-layer-effect-tools:
    description: Layer effect tools — set_blend_mode, set_shadow, set_tint, set_motion_path, set_clip_path, edit_visual (supports sourceRect, spritesheet, frameIndex)
    file: src/tools/layer-effects.ts
  mcp-state-config-tools:
    description: State configuration tools — set_audio, configure_transition, set_state_parent with cycle detection
    file: src/tools/state-config.ts
  mcp-export-tools:
    description: Export tools — export_svg (via @atelier/svg) and export_lottie (via @atelier/lottie)
    file: src/tools/export.ts
  mcp-asset-tools:
    description: Asset management tools — add_asset, list_assets, remove_asset with usage tracking
    file: src/tools/assets.ts
  mcp-variable-tools:
    description: Variable management tools — add_variable, list_variables, remove_variable with usage tracking
    file: src/tools/variables.ts
  mcp-interaction-tools:
    description: Interaction tools — add_interaction, list_interactions, remove_interaction for trigger-action bindings
    file: src/tools/interactions.ts
  mcp-ref-tools:
    description: Ref layer tools — set_ref (source reference with self-reference prevention), resolve_refs (check in-memory resolution status)
    file: src/tools/refs.ts
  mcp-performance-tools:
    description: Performance tools — profile (frame timing), diff_frames (change detection), batch_preview (multi-frame), complexity (document analysis)
    file: src/tools/performance.ts
  mcp-overlay-tools:
    description: Overlay layer tools — add_handle, add_page_number; tag-isolated TextVisual overlays for social-feed compositions
    file: src/tools/overlays.ts
  mcp-recipe-tools:
    description: Studio Recipe tools — recipe_list/get/validate/save/apply. Wraps the recipe load/validate/serialize/applyRecipeToOverlay pipeline (re-implemented locally on @a-company/atelier-schema + yaml to avoid a cli↔mcp dependency cycle). save refuses invalid recipes; apply wires overlay_rules only (trim/transcribe/caption application stays CLI-only)
    file: src/tools/recipes.ts
  mcp-import-images:
    description: Folder image ingestion — atelier_import_images lists images in a directory, registers assets, and optionally creates centered ImageVisual layers (mirrors the Studio image-drop layer-building + welcome-background-swap convention; defers natural-dimension measurement so bounds default to a centered min(canvas.w, canvas.h) square)
    file: src/tools/import-images.ts
  mcp-mind-map:
    description: Mind-map query stub — atelier_mind_map_query walks <projectDir>/.atelier/mind-map/ (preferred), assets/, or projectDir itself and returns local file paths whose extension matches a slot kind (image/video/audio/font/voice/logo; text returns empty with a note). Optional hints narrow by filename or ancestor dir name within the search root, OR'd. Sorted by mtime, depth-capped at 4, pure read against local disk. Phase 4 builds the indexed/curated version.
    file: src/tools/mind-map.ts
    gates:
      - ^valid-mind-map-query
  # ── v1.0 clip tools (Slice A) ──────
  mcp-tool-add-clip:
    description: atelier_add_clip — register a media source as a clip layer on a video or audio track via disk round-trip. Probes duration through an injectable probeDurationFn, derives a slug-based id (clip-<slug> or aud-<slug>), lazy-creates the track group, and recomputes the derived timeline. Idempotent — re-adding the same source preserves placement and applies only explicit startFrame/sourceOffset/sourceEnd overrides. Writes back to disk + store.set(source="llm").
    file: src/tools/clips.ts
  mcp-tool-move-clip:
    description: atelier_move_clip — shift a clip's composition-frame startFrame. Captions parented to the clip stay aligned (renderer uses clip-local time). Recomputes the timeline summary block. Round-trips through disk.
    file: src/tools/clips.ts
  mcp-tool-trim-clip:
    description: atelier_trim_clip — adjust sourceOffset / sourceEnd (seconds-into-source) on a clip. Captions outside the new effective range are NOT auto-pruned; the renderer skips out-of-range deltas naturally. Requires at least one of the two fields.
    file: src/tools/clips.ts
  mcp-tool-remove-clip:
    description: atelier_remove_clip — drop a clip layer plus all transitively-parented descendants (caption layers, etc.), strip referencing deltas across every state, and remove the matching assets entry. Refuses to remove a track group layer (use atelier_remove_track in a future release).
    file: src/tools/clips.ts
  mcp-tool-transcribe-clip:
    description: atelier_transcribe_clip — (re)build per-clip caption layers as cap-<slug>-N parented to the clip layer. Refuses audio layers (audio captions not supported in v1). Production wiring receives a transcribeFn via __setTranscribeClipFn; tests stub the same hook. Fallback reads an existing transcript at <projectDir>/transcripts/<stem>.json.
    file: src/tools/clips.ts
  mcp-tool-move-slide:
    description: atelier_move_slide — splice-reorder a carousel project's slides[] array. Refuses on non-carousel projects and on out-of-bounds indices. Pure-data mutation, disk-only (no derived re-render).
    file: src/tools/clips.ts
  mcp-lib-timeline-ops:
    description: Local duplication of cli/lib/timeline-ops.ts plus slugifyBasename / buildCaptionLayers / probeDuration. Lives here so the MCP clip tools have access without forming a cli↔mcp cycle. Mirrors the duplication convention used by recipes.ts / overlays.ts / effective-transcript.ts / media-notes.ts. MUST be kept in sync with cli/lib/timeline-ops.ts until the planned Unit-0.5 lift into a shared package.
    file: src/lib/timeline-ops.ts
  # ── v1.0 rename cascade (Slice C) ──────
  mcp-tool-rename-media:
    description: 'atelier_rename_media — MCP wrapper around #rename-media renameMedia with workspace scoping. Validates oldBasename + newBasename via isValidMediaBasenameForRename (rejects separators, "." / "..", leading dot, control chars, empty) — the single line of defense because renameMedia joins straight into <projectDir>/media/<basename> with no further sanitization. Bounds the rename to workspaceDir (defaults to process.cwd()): rejects any projectDir that resolves outside the workspace root via resolve()+prefix check with sep boundary — closes Aegis Finding 1 (TD-2026-05-27). On success and !dryRun, reloads <projectDir>/project.atelier into the DocumentStore via store.set(documentId, parsedDoc, "system") so subsequent tool calls see the post-rename state. Wraps any thrown error in the standard `{ error }` envelope with isError:true. destructiveHint:true.'
    file: src/tools/rename-media.ts
    gates: ['^valid-media-basename', '^workspace-scoped-project-dir']
    signals: ['!media-rename-cascaded']
    tags: [rename, media, cascade, mcp, security, v1]
  mcp-lib-rename-media:
    description: 'Local duplication of cli/lib/rename-media.ts (renameMedia + applyMediaRenameToDoc + scanArtifactsForOldBasename + isValidMediaBasenameForRename). Lives here so the MCP rename tool has access without forming a cli↔mcp dependency cycle. Mirrors the duplication convention established by mcp-lib-timeline-ops / recipes.ts / overlays.ts. Carries a sentinel header comment explaining the dep-cycle constraint and the in-sync-with-cli requirement; the two files MUST be edited together until the planned Unit-0.5 lift into a shared package.'
    file: src/lib/rename-media.ts
    tags: [rename, media, lib, duplication, v1]
  # ── v1.0.x doc-management tools (Slice B) ──────
  mcp-tool-create-doc:
    description: 'atelier_create_doc — programmatic doc creation for video / image / carousel kinds at a project root OR as a slide of an existing carousel (asCarouselSlide:true + carouselDocPath). Gates: ^valid-doc-name (isValidDocName on the user-supplied name), ^manifest-doc-protected (refuses to create a doc named "project.atelier"), and ^workspace-scoped-doc-tool (projectDir must resolve inside workspaceDir, defaulting to process.cwd()). On success, composes the doc via the cli twin''s composeImage|Video|Carousel and writes <projectDir>/<slug>.atelier with collision-suffixing; when appending to a carousel, uses the v1 simple-cycle check (see ~doc-cycle-v1-simple-check).'
    file: src/tools/docs.ts
    gates: ['^valid-doc-name', '^manifest-doc-protected', '^workspace-scoped-doc-tool']
    tags: [doc, mcp-tool, create, v1.0.x]
  mcp-tool-duplicate-doc:
    description: 'atelier_duplicate_doc — file-level duplicate with collision-suffixing (-2, -3, …). Optional appendSlideRef appends the duplicate as a SlideRef on the host carousel (v1 simple-cycle check). Gates: ^valid-doc-name (basename), ^manifest-doc-protected (refuses to duplicate project.atelier), ^workspace-scoped-doc-tool, ^doc-path-inside-project. Idempotent on a no-op same-name duplicate? No — collision-suffixing guarantees a fresh path.'
    file: src/tools/docs.ts
    gates: ['^valid-doc-name', '^manifest-doc-protected', '^workspace-scoped-doc-tool', '^doc-path-inside-project']
    tags: [doc, mcp-tool, duplicate, v1.0.x]
  mcp-tool-delete-doc:
    description: 'atelier_delete_doc — workspace-wide cascade. Walks every sibling project subdir under workspaceDir; removes matching SlideRef entries from any carousel manifest; collects dangling RefVisual layers into a report (NOT auto-removed per ~doc-dangling-refvisual-reported); unlinks the doc. Gates: ^manifest-doc-protected (isManifestDoc refuses project.atelier), ^workspace-scoped-doc-tool, ^doc-path-inside-project. destructiveHint:true.'
    file: src/tools/docs.ts
    gates: ['^manifest-doc-protected', '^workspace-scoped-doc-tool', '^doc-path-inside-project']
    tags: [doc, mcp-tool, delete, cascade, v1.0.x]
  mcp-tool-list-docs:
    description: 'atelier_list_docs — enumerate the manifest + carousel slides[] + every other root-level *.atelier in a project as DocListEntry[]. Read-only; ^workspace-scoped-doc-tool only. statSync follows symlinks (~doc-symlink-followed). The single line of truth for the studio sidebar''s DOCUMENT / SLIDES / OTHER DOCS groups when fetched via MCP.'
    file: src/tools/docs.ts
    gates: ['^workspace-scoped-doc-tool']
    tags: [doc, mcp-tool, list, v1.0.x]
  mcp-lib-doc-management:
    description: 'Intentional duplicate of cli/src/lib/doc-management.ts. Lives here so the MCP doc tools have access without forming a cli↔mcp dependency cycle — the same convention as mcp-lib-rename-media / mcp-lib-timeline-ops / recipes.ts / overlays.ts. Carries a sentinel header comment explaining the dep-cycle constraint and the in-sync-with-cli requirement. ONE INTENTIONAL DIVERGENCE: createDoc / duplicateDoc here use a SIMPLER cycle check (see ~doc-cycle-v1-simple-check) — "is src already in slides[]?" — instead of the full transitive walk; everything else stays in lockstep with the cli twin.'
    file: src/lib/doc-management.ts
    tags: [doc, lib, duplication, v1.0.x]
  mcp-lib-doc-management-types:
    description: 'Intentional duplicate of cli/src/lib/doc-management-types.ts (DocKind, CreateDocOptions, DuplicateDocOptions, DeleteDocOptions, DocListEntry, DocDeleteCascadeReport, DocDuplicateReport, isValidDocName, isManifestDoc). Pure types + validators — zero I/O. Lives here for the same dep-cycle reason as mcp-lib-doc-management; the two files MUST be edited together with their cli twins until the planned Unit-0.5 lift into a shared package.'
    file: src/lib/doc-management-types.ts
    tags: [doc, types, lib, duplication, v1.0.x]
signals:
  '!clip-added-to-track':
    description: 'Declared signal for the v1.0 clip tools — fires when atelier_add_clip lands a new clip layer onto a video or audio track. NOT yet wired to an emitter; reserved as the ambient WS-bridge layer that will fan out clip additions to attached studio instances in a future pass. Listed here so the symbol registry has the canonical name before the wiring lands.'
    emittedBy: ["mcp-tool-add-clip"]
    tags: [clip, timeline, future, ambient, v1]
  '!media-rename-cascaded':
    description: 'Emitted by atelier_rename_media after a successful rename cascade (media file + transcript + project.atelier all written, rollback not triggered). Currently informational — the MCP tool already reloads the doc via store.set(source:"system") so subscribers can detect via the !doc-change stream — but declared explicitly so the rename surface has a dedicated symbol for future ambient layers (notifications, undo records, audit trail).'
    emittedBy: ["mcp-tool-rename-media"]
    tags: [rename, media, cascade, v1]
gates:
  ^workspace-scoped-project-dir:
    description: 'atelier_rename_media bounds the rename to the workspace root: by default process.cwd() (the MCP server is launched from the workspace), or an explicit `workspaceDir` argument. Any projectDir that resolves outside that root is rejected with `projectDir must be inside workspace <root>` before any cascade work runs. Resolved-prefix containment check with a trailing path separator boundary, so sibling /a/workspace-x does NOT pass for workspace /a/workspace. Closes Aegis Finding 1 (TD-2026-05-27): the MCP tool previously accepted an unconstrained projectDir.'
    enforcement: resolve()+startsWith(root + sep) containment check
    appliesTo: ["mcp-tool-rename-media"]
  # ── v1.0.x doc-management gates ──────
  ^workspace-scoped-doc-tool:
    description: 'The MCP doc tools (atelier_create_doc / atelier_duplicate_doc / atelier_delete_doc / atelier_list_docs) require projectDir / (workspaceDir + projectName) to resolve inside workspaceDir, which defaults to process.cwd() (the MCP server is launched from the workspace). resolveProjectInWorkspace() does resolve()+startsWith(workspaceAbs + sep) containment check, rejecting any projectDir that escapes the workspace root. Mirrors ^workspace-scoped-project-dir from rename-media; the closing-of-Aegis-Finding-1 posture is now uniform across every workspace-scoped MCP tool.'
    enforcement: resolveProjectInWorkspace() resolve()+startsWith containment check
    appliesTo: ["mcp-tool-create-doc", "mcp-tool-duplicate-doc", "mcp-tool-delete-doc", "mcp-tool-list-docs"]
aspects:
  store-synchronous-registration-order-emit:
    description: 'onChange listeners fire synchronously inside create/set/delete (not on a microtask), in registration order, over a slice() snapshot of the listener array taken at emit time — so a listener that subscribes/unsubscribes mid-emit neither skips nor double-fires its siblings. The unsubscribe closure splices by indexOf, so the same function registered twice only removes one copy.'
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - event-emitter
      - ordering
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:106-127
    enforcement: snapshot listener list before iterating
    appliesTo: ["mcp-store"]
  store-listener-failure-isolation:
    description: 'emit wraps each listener in its own try/catch and swallows the error, so one buggy subscriber cannot break the mutation chain for the rest — but the failure is also silently lost (no logger is wired into this package yet). A future maintainer debugging a dropped bridge broadcast should suspect a throwing listener here.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - gotcha
      - resilience
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:118-126
    enforcement: per-listener try/catch swallow
    appliesTo: ["mcp-store"]
  store-default-source-system:
    description: 'create/set/delete default the MutationSource to "system" when the caller omits it, NOT "human" or "llm". Tools that mutate via store.set without a tag (e.g. the overlay tools) therefore emit source="system", which the studio bridge treats as silent (no re-broadcast) — only explicit source="llm" writes (import-images, recipe apply) round-trip to the browser.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - default
      - live-bridge
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:46
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:62
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:68
    enforcement: default parameter = "system"
    appliesTo: ["mcp-store"]
  store-single-instance-shared:
    description: 'createServer accepts an optional DocumentStore so the CLI can spawn one McpServer per WebSocket connection while sharing ONE store across all of them — every client''s writes surface through the single onChange emitter the live bridge subscribes to. Pass nothing and each server gets an isolated in-memory store instead.'
    tags:
      - architecture
      - core-invariant
      - live-bridge
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/index.ts:75-77
      - packages/mcp/src/index.ts:65-74
    enforcement: optional shared-store parameter
    appliesTo: ["mcp-store"]
  document-validate-after-construction:
    description: 'atelier_create runs validateDocument on the freshly-built doc (and atelier_load runs parseAtelier, which validates) BEFORE store.create — the document tools are the ONLY tools that schema-validate. Every other mutating tool (layers, shapes, deltas, effects, etc.) writes unvalidated into the live document, so a malformed mutation is only caught later by atelier_validate or at resolve time. Known inconsistency.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - fail-fast
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/document.ts:50-53
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/document.ts:102-105
    enforcement: validateDocument/parseAtelier before create
    appliesTo: ["mcp-document-tools"]
  document-export-raw-yaml-result:
    description: 'atelier_export returns the serialized YAML as a bare text content block (not the JSON {success,...} envelope used by every other tool), so a caller parsing tool output must special-case export — its payload IS the document, not a status wrapper.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - gotcha
      - serialization
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/document.ts:124-125
    enforcement: raw-text content block
    appliesTo: ["mcp-document-tools"]
  layer-mutate-in-place-no-set:
    description: 'add/edit/remove/reorder mutate the document object returned by store.get directly and never call store.set, relying on store.get handing back the live reference. onChange therefore NEVER fires for layer edits — the studio bridge will not see them until some OTHER tool calls store.set. This diverges from the root ~copy-on-write-doc convention, which only import-images / recipe-apply actually follow.'
    tags:
      - gotcha
      - mutation
      - live-bridge
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layers.ts:129
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layers.ts:163-181
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layers.ts:219
    enforcement: direct in-place mutation, no store.set
    appliesTo: ["mcp-layer-tools"]
  layer-reorder-clamps-overshoot:
    description: 'atelier_reorder clamps the target index with Math.min(position, layers.length - 1), so a position past the end silently lands the layer at the top of the stack rather than erroring. Combined with painters-order rendering, an out-of-range reorder quietly brings a layer fully forward.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - clamp
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layers.ts:273-275
    enforcement: Math.min clamp to length-1
    appliesTo: ["mcp-layer-tools"]
  layer-parent-existence-not-cycle:
    description: 'add/edit_layer only checks that a parentId refers to an existing layer — it does NOT detect a parent cycle (A→B→A). Transform-inheritance cycle protection lives downstream in the canvas renderer''s visited-Set guard, not at authoring time here.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - validation
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layers.ts:109-111
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layers.ts:171-178
    enforcement: existence check only, no cycle scan
    appliesTo: ["mcp-layer-tools"]
  shape-visual-type-guard:
    description: 'set_shape/set_fill/set_stroke refuse to run unless layer.visual.type === "shape", returning a typed error naming the actual type — they never coerce a text/image/ref layer into a shape. The mutation casts through ShapeVisual after the guard.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - type-guard
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/shapes.ts:53
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/shapes.ts:90
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/shapes.ts:120
    enforcement: visual.type === "shape" guard
    appliesTo: ["mcp-shape-tools"]
  state-remove-cascades-deltas:
    description: 'atelier_remove_state deletes the whole state entry including all its deltas and reports deltasRemoved — there is no orphan-delta cleanup elsewhere because deltas live INSIDE the state. add_state rejects a duplicate name; edit_state only patches provided fields.'
    tags:
      - cascade
      - mutation
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/states.ts:99-100
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/states.ts:40-42
    enforcement: delete state key drops nested deltas
    appliesTo: ["mcp-state-tools"]
  delta-add-validates-range-then-overlap:
    description: 'add_delta fails fast on an inverted range (start > end) BEFORE building the delta, then runs validateNoOverlap against the existing state deltas. edit_delta re-validates by first filtering the edited delta OUT of the list (filter i !== deltaIndex) so a delta never reports overlapping with itself.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - fail-fast
      - core-invariant
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/deltas.ts:62-64
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/deltas.ts:79-82
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/deltas.ts:138-142
    enforcement: range guard + self-excluded overlap check
    appliesTo: ["mcp-delta-tools"]
  delta-preset-all-or-nothing:
    description: 'apply_preset expands the preset to deltas, validates EVERY new delta for overlap, and pushes NONE if any one overlaps (errors accumulated then returned) — the preset application is atomic, never partially applied.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - atomicity
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/deltas.ts:218-232
    enforcement: validate-all-before-push-any
    appliesTo: ["mcp-delta-tools"]
  preset-deltas-min-one:
    description: 'define_preset requires at least one delta (schema .min(1)) and lazily creates doc.presets on first define. It does not validate that the preset properties are animatable beyond the per-delta schema, nor that referenced layers exist — presets are layer-agnostic until expanded by apply_preset.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - convention
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/presets.ts:45
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/presets.ts:53
    enforcement: schema min(1) + lazy presets init
    appliesTo: ["mcp-preset-tools"]
  preview-validate-splits-error-classes:
    description: 'atelier_validate reports schema errors and delta-overlap errors as SEPARATE arrays (schemaErrors vs overlapErrors, overlaps checked per state) and is only valid when both are empty — overlap is not a schema concern, so a schema-clean doc can still be invalid.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - convention
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/preview.ts:39-51
    enforcement: dual-array error split
    appliesTo: ["mcp-preview-tools"]
  preview-returns-base-and-computed:
    description: 'atelier_preview returns BOTH each layer''s base frame/bounds/opacity/rotation AND its computedProperties for the frame, so the AI can see the static authored values layered against the animated overrides rather than only the resolved result. Resolution errors are caught and returned as an error result, not thrown.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - introspection
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/preview.ts:86-94
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/preview.ts:102-104
    enforcement: emit base + computed per layer
    appliesTo: ["mcp-preview-tools"]
  template-instantiate-creates-new-doc:
    description: 'atelier_instantiate_template creates a brand-NEW store entry from the instantiation result and leaves the source template document untouched — it does not mutate or replace the template in place. The core instantiateTemplate strips the variables block, so the new doc is no longer a template.'
    tags:
      - immutability
      - templates
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/templates.ts:38-44
    enforcement: store.create new doc, template preserved
    appliesTo: ["mcp-template-tools"]
  template-find-vars-classifies:
    description: 'atelier_find_variables cross-references discovered {{var}} references against declared doc.variables to return undeclared (referenced-but-missing) and unused (declared-but-unreferenced) sets — a lint-style report, not a mutation.'
    tags:
      - introspection
      - templates
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/templates.ts:66-74
    enforcement: set-difference of referenced vs declared
    appliesTo: ["mcp-template-tools"]
  effect-null-clears-property:
    description: 'set_blend_mode / set_shadow / set_tint / set_motion_path / set_clip_path all treat an explicit null argument as "remove" (delete layer.<prop>) versus an object as "set". null is the documented clear signal — omitting the field is not the same as passing null.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - api
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layer-effects.ts:50-55
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layer-effects.ts:83-88
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layer-effects.ts:152-157
    enforcement: null → delete, object → assign
    appliesTo: ["mcp-layer-effect-tools"]
  effect-edit-visual-type-gated-fields:
    description: 'edit_visual gates each field group by visual type — content/style only on text, src/assetId/sourceRect/spritesheet/frameIndex only on image, shape/fill/stroke only on shape — erroring per-field on a mismatch. style is a PARTIAL merge (Object.assign over the existing style, only provided keys overwritten); sourceRect/spritesheet accept null to remove. Empty update set is an error.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - type-guard
      - merge
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layer-effects.ts:258-267
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layer-effects.ts:281-300
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/layer-effects.ts:324-326
    enforcement: per-field type guard + partial style merge
    appliesTo: ["mcp-layer-effect-tools"]
  state-config-own-cycle-detector:
    description: 'set_state_parent walks the parent chain with its own visited-Set cycle detector (seeded with the state being edited) and rejects a parent assignment that would close a loop — a deliberate re-implementation of core''s resolveAncestorChain guard, kept here because the mcp package does not reach into core for authoring-time validation.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - validation
      - core-invariant
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/state-config.ts:130-139
    enforcement: visited-set walk + reject cycle
    appliesTo: ["mcp-state-config-tools"]
  state-config-transition-self-and-prune:
    description: 'configure_transition refuses a self-transition (stateName === targetState) and requires the target state to exist; removing a transition deletes the target key and, when the transitions map empties, deletes the whole transitions object so an empty map never lingers.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - cleanup
      - edge-case
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/state-config.ts:72-87
    enforcement: self-guard + empty-map prune
    appliesTo: ["mcp-state-config-tools"]
  export-defaults-first-state-frame-zero:
    description: 'export_svg and export_lottie default the state to the FIRST key of doc.states (Object.keys insertion order) and the frame to 0 when omitted — so which frame/state you get is order-sensitive on the states map. Both wrap the renderer call in try/catch and return any failure as an error result.'
    tags:
      - default
      - ordering
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/export.ts:43-51
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/export.ts:60-62
    enforcement: first-key default + frame 0
    appliesTo: ["mcp-export-tools"]
  asset-usage-tracked-not-enforced:
    description: 'remove_asset deletes the asset even when layers (ImageVisual.assetId) or state audio (audio.src === assetId) still reference it — it only WARNS, never blocks. add_asset rejects a duplicate id and lazily creates doc.assets. Usage is reported, dangling references are the caller''s problem.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - referential-integrity
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/assets.ts:113-134
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/assets.ts:47-48
    enforcement: warn-on-dangling, never block
    appliesTo: ["mcp-asset-tools"]
  variable-remove-warns-and-prunes:
    description: 'remove_variable deletes a declared variable even if {{references}} still exist (warning only), and when the last variable is removed it sets doc.variables = undefined rather than leaving an empty object — so "has variables" stays a truthy check downstream. add_variable rejects duplicates and lazily inits the map.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - cleanup
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/variables.ts:101-108
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/variables.ts:41-42
    enforcement: warn-on-referenced + undefined-on-empty
    appliesTo: ["mcp-variable-tools"]
  interaction-trigger-action-field-validation:
    description: 'add_interaction validates trigger- and action-specific required fields beyond the schema — timer needs delay, signal needs a signal name, go-to-state needs an existing target state, set-variable needs both variable and value, toggle-visibility''s optional targetLayer must exist. Duplicate interaction ids per layer are rejected, and the interactions array is pruned to undefined when emptied.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - fail-fast
      - cleanup
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/interactions.ts:60-84
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/interactions.ts:56-58
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/interactions.ts:158-160
    enforcement: per-trigger/per-action required-field checks
    appliesTo: ["mcp-interaction-tools"]
  ref-self-only-not-transitive:
    description: 'set_ref rejects ONLY a direct self-reference (src === id) — it does not detect a transitive ref cycle (A→B→A). resolve_refs is read-only and reports per-ref in-memory resolution status (target name/layer/state counts) without resolving the referenced content.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - validation
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/refs.ts:43
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/refs.ts:66-83
    enforcement: src === id guard only
    appliesTo: ["mcp-ref-tools"]
  performance-diff-strict-inequality:
    description: 'diff_frames flags a property as changed using strict !== over the union of both frames'' computed-property keys — so object-valued properties differ by IDENTITY, not deep equality, and two structurally-equal objects can be reported as a (false) change. profile/batch_preview round performance.now() ms to 3 decimals; batch_preview caps frames at 60 via schema.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - gotcha
      - magic-number
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/performance.ts:117-123
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/performance.ts:70
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/performance.ts:143
    enforcement: strict !== compare + frame cap 60
    appliesTo: ["mcp-performance-tools"]
  performance-complexity-depth-guard:
    description: 'complexity computes max state-hierarchy depth by walking each state''s parent chain with a per-walk visited Set, so a (mis-authored) parent cycle terminates the walk instead of looping forever. Expression count is detected by the {expr} shape on a delta''s from/to value.'
    tags:
      - edge-case
      - introspection
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/performance.ts:243-254
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/performance.ts:217-220
    enforcement: visited-set bounded chain walk
    appliesTo: ["mcp-performance-tools"]
  overlay-tag-isolation-but-mutates-in-place:
    description: 'add_handle / add_page_number tag emitted layers "overlay" so the recipe pipeline''s applyRecipeToOverlay drops only overlay-tagged layers on re-run — but unlike import-images/recipe-apply these tools mutate via doc.layers.push and then call store.set(id, doc) on the SAME reference (no copy-on-write, default source="system"). They reject a duplicate layer id before pushing.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - mutation
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/overlays.ts:140-141
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/overlays.ts:125-127
    enforcement: tag "overlay" + in-place push + set
    appliesTo: ["mcp-overlay-tools"]
  overlay-anchor-corner-math:
    description: 'anchorToFrame maps the four corners to a frame position inset by margin AND a matching normalized anchorPoint (e.g. top-right → x = canvas.width - margin, anchorPoint {1,0}) so the text box hugs the corner regardless of its own size. The default margin is 24px and default text style is Inter/24/600/#F5F5F7.'
    tags:
      - geometry
      - convention
      - magic-number
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/overlays.ts:55-73
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/overlays.ts:39-45
    enforcement: corner → frame + anchorPoint pair
    appliesTo: ["mcp-overlay-tools"]
  overlay-page-format-regex-duplicated:
    description: 'renderPageNumberFormat substitutes {current}/{total} plus zero-pad forms {current:02d}/{total:02d} via the regex \{(current|total)(?::0(\d+)d)?\} — an INTENTIONAL byte-for-byte duplicate of recipes.ts''s same function, kept duplicated to avoid a cli↔mcp dependency cycle. Edit one, edit the other.'
    tags:
      - duplication
      - convention
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/overlays.ts:90-103
    enforcement: regex substitution (mirror of recipes.ts)
    appliesTo: ["mcp-overlay-tools"]
  recipe-save-refuses-invalid:
    description: 'recipe_save validates the recipe (object or YAML text) BEFORE writing and REFUSES to persist an invalid one, returning the validation errors and creating parent dirs only on the success path — invalid recipes never touch disk. recipe_validate accepts either a path or inline yaml and reports parse failures as validation errors rather than throwing.'
    tags:
      - validation
      - fail-fast
      - core-invariant
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:392-405
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:347-355
    enforcement: validate-before-write, refuse invalid
    appliesTo: ["mcp-recipe-tools"]
  recipe-apply-overlay-only-copy-on-write:
    description: 'recipe_apply applies ONLY overlay_rules (handle + page-number) — silence-trim / transcribe / caption sections are silently ignored (CLI-only). It is tag-isolated (drops prior "overlay" layers, re-adds fresh) and copy-on-write (builds a new doc, never mutates in place) then store.set with source="llm". page_number requires currentIndex+totalCount or the layer is skipped with a warning.'
    tags:
      - scoping
      - convention
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:143-169
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:452-456
    enforcement: overlay_rules-only, tag-isolated, copy-on-write
    appliesTo: ["mcp-recipe-tools"]
  recipe-path-resolution-precedence:
    description: 'resolveRecipePath loads absolute/slash-bearing references literally, but a bare name is resolved against <projectDir>/.atelier/recipes/ FIRST, then ~/.atelier/recipes/, trying extensions in a fixed order (.recipe.yaml/.recipe.json/.yaml/.yml/.json). recipe_list de-dupes by basename with project recipes winning over user recipes. Mirrors the CLI''s resolveRecipePath (re-implemented to avoid the cli↔mcp cycle).'
    tags:
      - convention
      - precedence
      - duplication
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:64-84
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:290-292
    enforcement: project-then-user dir, fixed ext order
    appliesTo: ["mcp-recipe-tools"]
  import-images-natural-dimension-fallback:
    description: 'import_images deliberately does NOT add an image-dimension dependency, so without measured natural dimensions each created layer''s bounds default to a centered min(canvas.width, canvas.height) square at canvas center with anchorPoint {0.5,0.5}. The limitation is surfaced both in the tool description and the response note.'
    tags:
      - gotcha
      - convention
      - default
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:128
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:158-165
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:187-189
    enforcement: centered min-dimension square fallback
    appliesTo: ["mcp-import-images"]
  import-images-background-swap-and-zstack:
    description: 'A single-image import whose doc layer[0].id === "background" replaces that welcome placeholder IN PLACE; otherwise each new layer is unshift-ed to index 0 so it paints at the BACK of the z-stack (renderer paints index 0 first), behind existing overlays — matching the Studio drop convention. The whole import is copy-on-write (new assets+layers, one store.set source="llm").'
    tags:
      - convention
      - ordering
      - edge-case
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:132
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:167-180
    enforcement: bg-swap guard + unshift-to-back
    appliesTo: ["mcp-import-images"]
  import-images-glob-and-dedup:
    description: 'matchesGlob is a single-segment matcher (no path separators) translating * → .* and ? → . over a regex-escaped pattern, case-insensitive, matching all when the glob is empty. deriveAssetId slugifies the filename stem and de-dupes collisions as `${base}-${n}` starting at n=2; layer ids follow the same `image-${n}` scheme. Results are sorted by localeCompare.'
    tags:
      - convention
      - dedup
      - edge-case
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:51-56
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:62-76
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:118-120
    enforcement: glob→regex + slug dedup -N
    appliesTo: ["mcp-import-images"]
  mind-map-query-local-only:
    description: 'atelier_mind_map_query is a pure read against local disk — no network surface, no external fetches, no store mutations. Per TD-271/TD-540 the creator''s mind-map never leaves their machine; the walk is rooted at the resolved projectDir and confined to its subtree. The DocumentStore parameter is accepted for register-function signature symmetry but is intentionally unused (a leading underscore on the parameter name documents this).'
    tags:
      - core-invariant
      - privacy
      - convention
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/mind-map.ts:170-172
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/mind-map.ts:148-160
    enforcement: pure read against local disk, _store unused
    appliesTo: ["mcp-mind-map"]
  mind-map-stub-no-ingestion:
    description: 'This is the Phase 3 STUB form of the mind-map. Every call re-walks the directory tree from scratch — there is no persistent index, no SQLite, no caching, no semantic search, no ingestion of arbitrary external dirs, and no `atelier mind-map reindex` CLI verb. Recency is approximated by mtime sort only. Phase 4 builds the indexed/curated version (TD-229/TD-271/TD-540). Walk order is first-existing-wins: .atelier/mind-map/ → assets/ → projectDir; depth capped at 4 levels below the chosen root to bound pathological recursion (deep nests, symlink loops).'
    tags:
      - scoping
      - convention
      - stub
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/mind-map.ts:85-94
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/mind-map.ts:106-141
    enforcement: walk-on-each-call, depth-capped at 4, no index
    appliesTo: ["mcp-mind-map"]
  # ── v1.0 bundle aspect ──────
  mcp-lib-duplication-vs-cli:
    description: 'Files in packages/mcp/src/lib/ that intentionally duplicate packages/cli/src/lib/ (timeline-ops.ts, rename-media.ts, doc-management.ts, doc-management-types.ts — and historically recipes.ts / overlays.ts / effective-transcript.ts / media-notes.ts) carry a sentinel header comment explaining the dep-cycle constraint and the in-sync requirement with the cli twin. The duplication is NOT an oversight: cli depends on mcp (the studio launches the MCP server in-process), so a cli→mcp import in the other direction would close a dependency cycle that breaks the build. Rule: when one twin changes behavior, the other MUST be updated in the same commit. The planned Unit-0.5 lift into a shared @a-company/atelier-ops package is the medium-term exit; until then, the duplication is the convention, not a bug. NOTE: the doc-management twin carries ONE INTENTIONAL behavioral divergence (~doc-cycle-v1-simple-check); everything else stays in lockstep.'
    tags:
      - duplication
      - dep-cycle
      - convention
      - core-invariant
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/lib/timeline-ops.ts:12
      - packages/mcp/src/lib/rename-media.ts:11
      - packages/mcp/src/lib/doc-management.ts:1-30
      - packages/mcp/src/lib/doc-management-types.ts:1-15
    enforcement: sentinel header comment + manual lockstep edit
    appliesTo: ["mcp-lib-timeline-ops", "mcp-lib-rename-media", "mcp-lib-doc-management", "mcp-lib-doc-management-types"]
  # ── v1.0.x doc-management bundle aspects ──────
  doc-cycle-v1-simple-check:
    description: 'The MCP twin of doc-management uses a SIMPLER cycle check than the cli twin: when createDoc / duplicateDoc append a SlideRef to a host carousel, it asks only "is the new src already present in slides[]?" — covering direct self-reference and duplicate inserts, but NOT a full transitive walk. The cli twin routes through composeCarouselProject which DOES run #ref-cycle detectCarouselCycle (full transitive cycle detection up to MAX_HOPS=64). The MCP twin documents this deviation in its header comments and intentionally accepts the gap as the v1 posture; full detection in the MCP path is the v1.1 follow-up. Practical impact: a creator who builds A→B→A via the MCP surface across two tool calls is not refused at the second call (the cli twin would refuse via composeCarouselProject); a single-call duplicate insert IS still refused.'
    tags:
      - doc
      - carousel
      - cycle
      - deviation
      - cautionary
      - v1.0.x
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/lib/doc-management.ts:170-180
      - packages/mcp/src/lib/doc-management.ts:212-220
    enforcement: 'is-src-already-in-slides predicate (no transitive walk)'
    appliesTo: ["mcp-lib-doc-management", "mcp-tool-create-doc", "mcp-tool-duplicate-doc"]
